  "body": "This matches Firefox, and the intent of this CSS pseudo-class, see\nhttps://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/4278.\n\n- [x] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * Firefox ships this.\n   * WebKit doesn't use `:focus` directly either because of Shadow DOM, but doesn't support `:focus-visible` yet.\n   * Chromium has a bug on file to change this (https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=1162070), but no official position yet from a Google employee, so we should get some (cc @alice @robdodson).\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/27015\n- [x] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/master/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chrome: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=1162070\n   * Firefox: N/A (has this behavior already)\n   * Safari: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=185859\n\nWe should also specify that `object`, `embed`, and `iframe` don't have outlines on focus by default, as that's the behavior Firefox, Chromium and WebKit have, but that's a separate patch / issue.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/6256/rendering.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jan 22, 2021, 4:55 PM UTC (6dcb992)\">/rendering.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/6256/e9d38e8...6dcb992/rendering.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jan 22, 2021, 4:55 PM UTC (6dcb992)\">diff</a> )",
